<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Granville Sharp</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1735">1735</a>–<a href="/years/1813">1813</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Granville Sharp was an English scholar and campaigner, one of the first British activists for the abolition of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/atlantic-slave-trade">slave trade</a>. He brought legal cases on behalf of enslaved Africans, including that of James <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/somerset">Somerset</a> in 1772. With the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/committee-for-the-relief-of-the-black-poor">Committee for the Relief of the Black Poor</a> he organised the settlement of the Province of Freedom in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sierra-leone">Sierra Leone</a> in 1787, and he later helped found the Society for Effecting the Abolition of the Slave Trade.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/granville-sharp.jpg" alt="Granville Sharp" width="320" height="374" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: G. Dance · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Granville_Sharp_(Hoare_memoire).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
